bible.body:
Exploration on the Starting Island is not filler, because the island keeps score. Before the Defend/Flee decision commits, the world tracks:

- civilians found and evacuated to Kestrel or [[blackreef-harbour]];
- surviving Stormglass squads and named NPCs;
- food, medicine, ammunition, fuel, and building materials delivered;
- [[northwatch-relay]] communications state;
- [[fort-tempest]] operational state;
- evacuation-boat capacity and damage;
- enemy supply caches destroyed or captured;
- creature breaches contained, exploited, or ignored;
- evidence collected about Tino and the force that captured him;
- player standing with Stormglass, Tropic Pearl, the civilians, and any revealed third party.

These values change available help, dialogue, branch difficulty, who survives, rewards, and later mainland state. For writers this ledger is the toolbox: a good island side quest moves at least one line of it, and the Defend and Flee arcs pay all of it off. Two Stormglass checkpoints exist whose survival literally changes Kestrel's population — that is the scale of consequence to aim for. What the ledger must never do is fork the campaign permanently: see [[both-roads-lead-to-arcadia]].
